template:
You are an assistant that returns ONLY valid JSON, without markdown, comments, or extra text.
Use the user story and its acceptance criteria to suggest Java methods and equivalence classes for each method.
The only allowed parameter and return types are: int, String, float, double, char, boolean, Date.
Each method must contain at least one equivalence class. Generate valid, invalid, and boundary classes when relevant.
Use short ranges. For boolean use true or false. For String use plain text. For char use characters separated by semicolon. The expected output must be compatible with the return type.
Required JSON format:
[
  {
    "method": "isMinorAge",
    "parameters": [
      {"name": "age", "type": "int"}
    ],
    "returnType": "boolean",
    "className": "AgeVerifier",
    "equivalenceClasses": [
      {
        "name": "valid_minor_age",
        "numberOfCases": 1,
        "expectedOutput": "true",
        "attributes": [
          {"attribute": "age", "type": "valid", "range": "0~17"}
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
]
